message.content:
I see something interesting in the `__libdwfl_elf_address_range` function. In the ET_REL case, there's a variable `first` that's declared as `bool first = true;` but it's only used in the `else` branch of the section layout. Let me look more carefully at the ET_REL case:

```c
bool first = true;
Elf_Scn *scn = NULL;
while ((scn = elf_nextscn (elf, scn)) != NULL)
{
    ...
    if (shdr->sh_flags & SHF_ALLOC)
    {
        ...
        if (shdr->sh_addr == 0 || ...)
        {
            // layout case
            ...
        }
        else
        {
            // already assigned case
            if (first || end < shdr->sh_addr + shdr->sh_size)
                end = shdr->sh_addr + shdr->sh_size;
            if (first || bias > shdr->sh_addr)
                bias = shdr->sh_addr;
            ...
        }
        first = false;
    }
}
```

Wait, `first` is initialized to `true` and set to `false` after each SHF_ALLOC section. But in the `if` branch (layout case), `first` is not used. In the `else` branch (already assigned case), `first` is used. This looks correct.

Let me look at the `process_elf` function in offline.c to understand the flow better.

